 "nifc.lows_verdict": {
  "computed_at": "2026-09-26T15:32:11+00:00",
  "definition": "Plain-language verdict on whether \"the lows rose too\" survives stricter tests, combining the NIFC floor-shift, rolling-minimum trend and 1983-85 sensitivity results with the FPA FOD 1992-2020 cross-check.",
  "n": null,
  "note": null,
  "source": "analysis.nifc",
  "unit": null,
  "value": "On the NIFC series, \"the lows rose too\" holds: the era-table floor rises 2.34x (1983-1999 min 1.15M to 2000-2025 min 2.69M acres), and the rolling 11-year minimum trends up with Kendall tau 0.51 (p=0.0001) against the window centre year, so the rise is not just the two 1988-vs-2020 endpoints v1 quoted. Dropping the earliest 1983-1985 years (the lowest points in the whole series, 1983-84 fire counts are separately flagged as anomalous) weakens it somewhat: the floor shift falls to 2.02x (1986-1999 min 1.33M vs the same 2000-2025 min 2.69M), because part of the original 1983-1999 floor was set by those specific early years. The claim survives this trim but is not as dramatic as the headline number once those years are set aside. On FPA FOD for the 1992-2020 overlap the floor also rises: FPA FOD min acres 2.02M (1992-1999) vs 3.53M (2000-2020), a 1.75x shift; NIFC and FPA FOD annual acres correlate at r=0.99 (Spearman rho=0.98) over the same 29 years, so FPA FOD is a noisier, reporting-limited echo of the same national total rather than an independent confirmation."
 },
